          "content": "# Branch Agnostic Stats\nAny given commit may be reachable from multiple branches. It may be reachable along a first-parent chain, or through a set of merges. However, there are associated properties independent of first-parent chains and independent of relative change compared to another branch. Examples of these properties are:\n\n* Git Host, Project, Commit SHA\n* Commit Type (merge, revert, standard)\n* Commit Author, Commit Time\n* Files Changed, Insertions, Deletions\n\nIn this context, Files Changed, Insertions, and Deletions are properties of the commit itself, as one can find in git show. This information in isolation does not indicate whether a downstream branch diverges or converges to an upstream branch. Similarly, each file modified as part of a commit has branch agnostic information, such as Insertions and Deletions made to the file.",
          "mode": "markdown"
        },
